Improvements: The landowner will be required to comply with Chapter 1.16 of the Cheyenne City
Code, which includes provisions for offsite improvements. Immediate improvements to the property
are not required. Subsequent development actions on this property may trigger additional
improvements to be made. The area is currently served by sanitary sewer (BOPU). Water service is
over one mile away to the northeast. The City and Board of Public Utilities have plans to construct a
water transmission line approximately one half mile south of the proposed annexation.  Public streets
built to an urban section are in place.

Platting: The area includes both platted and unplatted land. Plats include EMJ Subdivision at the
southeast corner of I-25 and College (Love’s), and Overland Trails, 1st, 2nd, 3rd, 4th, and 5th Filings at
the southwest corner of I-25 and College and part of the northwest corner (McDonalds). Unplatted
properties include the State property at the northwest corner of I-25 and College and the Diamond
Shamrock and adjacent parcels at the northeast corner of I-25 and College.

Zoning:  The property is currently zoned P, Public, PUD, Planned Unit Development, and CB,
Commercial Business.

