City Surveyor:
1. The “Landowners” for the two parcels of land located in the NE1/4
of Section 14 under the Laramie County Assessors records as:
a. State PIN Number 13671410000300 (Total Petroleum, Inc.)
b. State PIN Number 13671410000099 (Swan Ranch, LLC)
Have been identified, but are delineated incorrectly as
projecting into the I-25 right of way.  This needs to be
corrected.

2. The WYDOT properties located north of West College Drive and West
of I-25 should also be labeled with the record boundary data per
the deed of record (Bk.1092, Pg.1163).

3. The lines of the “UNPLATTED” area on this map in Wyoming State
Highway Commission ownership represent the surveyed lines of
apparent occupation, but do not adequately represent boundaries
or legal descriptions of record in accordance with the
requirements of the annexation statutes under W.S. 15-1-401 thru
15-1-423.  The legal description of record under the Quit Claim
Deed recorded in BK.1092, Pg.1163, is not in agreement with the
legal description provided on this map.  Therefore, in my
professional opinion, the boundaries are uncertain or incapable
of ascertainment (at present).

W.S. 15-1-413   Survey of boundaries; when and how to be made; presumption once recorded.

(a)  If the boundaries of any city or town are uncertain or incapable of ascertainment and upon the
change in boundaries of any city or town pursuant to any annexation under this chapter, the governing
body, by ordinance, shall provide for a survey thereof.  When the survey is made, the boundaries shall be
marked by substantial monuments, and the person making the survey shall report to the governing body
describing the boundaries by metes and bounds.  The description as nearly as possible shall refer, if upon
surveyed lands, to the corners or lines of the United States surveys.  The person making the survey shall
also file with the city or town clerk the field notes of his survey.  The city or town clerk shall then file a
copy of the report and a copy of the field notes certified by the mayor and clerk with the county clerk for
the county in which the city or town is located.

(b)  Any survey or perambulation made and recorded as provided in subsection (a) of this section
is presumptive of the boundaries of the city or town, and any copy thereof certified by the county clerk
shall be received in evidence in any court of this state.
