as follows:

4. With the known discrepancies between the legal description of
record under the Quit Claim Deed (BK.1092, Pg.1163) and the
attempt to further depict and accurately survey the lines of
occupation under this survey, it is in my opinion very clear that
the true boundaries are most certainly “UNCERTAIN”.  In my
opinion, the Statute implies that the survey is to be used in
accomplishing identification and resolution of these
discrepancies.  I believe these uncertainties need to be resolved
prior to approval of this annexation.  Or in the very least (not
my recommendation), a formal “REPORT” specifically identifying
and describing the uncertainties of the boundary identification
to be recorded with this annexation map.  I have not seen such a
report.  Otherwise, with the recording of this annexation map,
the City is knowingly and willfully certifying to the creation of
a conflict of legal descriptions in the public record, which may
or may not eventually change the City boundaries with resolution
of the discrepancies.

5. In the “CERTIFICATE OF SURVEYOR” Mr. Steil does not state that
this Annexation Map was prepared from “… a survey made by him”.
However, in the “LEGEND” he shows survey monuments having been
set by himself.  The “CERTIFICATE OF SURVEYOR” should be amended
accordingly.

6. On page 6 and on page 8 of the BUILDING AND DEVELOPMENT OFFICE –
ANNEXATION INFORMATION handout the following policy requirement
is recited “…a plat of all the real property described herein has
previously been filed with the County Clerk and Ex-Officio
Register of Deeds for Laramie County, Wyoming.”  Has this policy
been waived?  If so, shouldn’t it be noted on the Annexation Map
along with any conditions attached?  Historically we have granted
such waivers for “UNPLATTED” lands with the condition that the
areas be platted prior to development.  However, all of these
“UNPLATTED” areas are already developed and we would have no
means of enforcing a platting requirement unless the area
development changes.

Response from Urban Planning to City Surveyor’s comments:
1. The map has been amended to address this comment.
2. This is addressed by the D1 note in the legend and the book and page notations on the
map.
