ANNEXATION REPORT DATA:  In compliance with 15-1-402 (c) the following information is
provided:

(i)
A map is not required for this report based on the absence of exercising the authority
granted under W.S. 15-3-202 (b) (ii).
(ii)
The total estimated cost of infrastructure improvements required of the landowners by
the City related to the annexation is approximately $0.  Additional improvements may
be required with subsequent development actions.
(iii)
Services customarily available to City residents include water, sewer, sanitation,
police and fire protection. Sewer service is available to the property currently; water
lines must be extended to the area in order to obtain City water service. Sanitation,
police and fire services will be available upon annexation. These services are
provided upon application and payment to the Board of Public Utilities, with
sanitation services occurring concurrently.  Provision of these services is initiated by
the property owner.
(iv)
Fees for water, sewer, and sanitation services are a variable amount for commercial
units, based upon volume.  Tap fees and for commercial units tap fees vary based on
the size of the tap required.
(v)
The current property tax mill levy imposed is 66.00 and projected property tax mill
levy imposed by the city is 71.00.
(vi)
The infrastructure described in (ii) above, includes improvements required within the
existing boundaries of the municipality to accommodate the proposed annexation.
